{"id":"9a564fd35615a768","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-elementary-chain.md","title":"Elementary Chain","display":"df-elementary-chain — Elementary Chain","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-elementary-chain","aliases":["17-df-elementary-chain"],"display":"df-elementary-chain — Elementary Chain","depends_on":["[[17-df-structure]]","[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[17-df-linear-order]]"],"source_section":"3.1","source_result":"Elementary-chain definition preceding Theorem 3.1.9","source_pages_print":[140],"source_pages_djvu":[156],"source_verification":"definition compared in supplied OCR; local extension from ordinal to nonempty linear indices used by theorem","label_origin":"local-catalog","legacy_label":"17-df-3.1.1","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-elementary-chain"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-elementary-chain</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-elementary-chain — Elementary Chain"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_section","html":"3.1"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Elementary-chain definition preceding Theorem 3.1.9"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>140</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>156</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"definition compared in supplied OCR; local extension from ordinal to nonempty linear indices used by theorem"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-df-3.1.1"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> 为集合，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"{&lt;}\\subseteq I\\times I\">\\({&lt;}\\subseteq I\\times I\\)</span> 为候选关系。\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> 是定义域为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span> 的集合函数，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak A_i=F(i)\">\\(\\mathfrak A_i=F(i)\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a>。\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\preceq_L\">\\(\\preceq_L\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}\">\\(\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"3f12d30db6793ecd\" href=\"?note=3f12d30db6793ecd\" title=\"17-df-linear-order\">17-df-linear-order</a>。\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L\\)</span> 的定义包括索引序与各分量的类型检验；此谓词允许空索引集。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I})\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\n\\land(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I}:I\\to\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\\forall i,j\\in I\\;(i&lt;j\\to\\mathfrak A_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak A_j).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{ElemChain}_L(I,&lt;,(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I})\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{StrictLinearOrder}(I,&lt;)\n\\land(\\mathfrak A_i)_{i\\in I}:I\\to\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\\forall i,j\\in I\\;(i&lt;j\\to\\mathfrak A_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak A_j).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The family typing and the elementary-inclusion condition are both part of the\npredicate.  Equality of indices needs no separate clause because\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A}_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak{A}_i\">\\(\\mathfrak{A}_i\\preceq_L\\mathfrak{A}_i\\)</span> follows from the definition.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-structure","status":"resolved","id":"fdac06af5a7f3bb5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-structure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-linear-order","status":"resolved","id":"3f12d30db6793ecd","anchor":"ref-3","target